course: dictionary
lesson: 1350
title: Canary: a bird, a colour, a warning
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A canary is a small yellow songbird, often kept as a pet. You can often work out a word's meaning from the words around it. «She keeps a canary, several piebald mice and a restless revolving squirrel.» The canary is one of her pets, because it sits in a list of animals she keeps.
explain: Canary can also mean a bright yellow colour. «The lovely canary-coloured cart lies on its side» and «a brand-new horse-drawn caravan, canary-yellow with green trim and red wheels» both describe colour, not a bird. Ask yourself: does the sentence describe a thing that sings, or something that looks yellow?
explain: Canary has a third meaning too. Long ago, coal miners carried canaries underground. If the bird got sick, the air was dangerous, so the miners left. Today, a canary in a coal mine means an early warning of danger.
fact: A canary is a small yellow songbird, and males are famous for their songs.
fact: Canaries are small finches, and they take their name from the Canary Islands.
fact: Canary yellow is a bright yellow colour, as in «canary-yellow with green trim».
fact: Long ago, coal miners took canaries underground, because a sick bird warned them that the air was bad.
fact: «A canary in a coal mine» means an early warning sign of danger.
exercise: «She keeps a canary, several piebald mice and a restless revolving squirrel.» In this sentence, what is a canary? | *A small yellow songbird kept as a pet | A cage with a turning wheel | A kind of coal | A cloth for the back of a chair
exercise: «The lovely canary-coloured cart lies on its side, smashed beyond repair.» In this sentence, what does canary-coloured mean? | Small and singing | *Bright yellow | Covered in coal dust | Green and red
exercise: Why did long ago coal miners carry canaries underground? | To carry the coal out | To count how many miners were down the mine | *To give an early warning if the air was dangerous | To sing to the miners and cheer them up
test: What does «a canary in a coal mine» mean? | A bird that lives inside a mine | *An early warning sign of danger | A bright yellow piece of coal | A miner's lunch box
test: What does canary yellow mean? | Dark grey, like coal | A type of birdcage | *A bright yellow colour | A loud song
exam: Which meaning of canary fits «The old Magpie says the night-air doesn't suit my throat, and a Canary calls its children to bed»? | An early warning of danger | *A small yellow songbird | A bright yellow colour | A cloth for the back of a chair
